Z||000001||LAMBO||11-10-2000||12:35 PM||||This is probably a dumb question, but was it on the compression stroke for #1 cylinder? Put you finger over the spark plug hole while tapping the starter over until you feel a good amount of air blow over it. This will be the compression stroke which is top dead center. You could have it on the exhaust stoke now. Just a thought.<BR>TL||||reg||1
Z||000002||Haze_Performance||11-10-2000||12:42 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LAMBO:<BR><B>This is probably a dumb question, but was it on the compression stroke for #1 cylinder? Put you finger over the spark plug hole while tapping the starter over until you feel a good amount of air blow over it. This will be the compression stroke which is top dead center. You could have it on the exhaust stoke now. Just a thought.<BR>TL</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> !!!!!!!!!! So if I didnt do it right.. Wounld it fix the problem if I just pulled out the Dis. and installed it 180 deg.?? <P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/goodlogo1_1.gif">   <BR><B>"AHHHHH!!! All Fiero's don't start on fire you BONEHEAD!!"</B>||||reg||11
Z||000003||StuGood||11-10-2000||01:29 PM||||Yep.  Think it's kind of traditional to install a distributor 180 degrees out the first time  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>||||reg||6
Z||000004||btoth||11-10-2000||01:56 PM||||is it possible that the wires aren't pluged into the dis.?  i've done that so many times when messing with the timming.  sometimes the one plug just falls out by itself on my car.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||11-10-2000||01:58 PM||||Haze, the distributor should have the connectors pointing towards the left rear of the car. Here is a pic of the firing order and plug locations on my car.<P>F=1<BR>E=2<BR>D=3<BR>C=4<BR>B=5<BR>A=6<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PlugW.jpg">  <BR><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 11-10-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Haze_Performance||11-10-2000||02:35 PM||||Ok ....Guys. Im going to 180 the Dis. Ill see if it works.||||reg||11
Z||000007||Haze_Performance||11-10-2000||04:01 PM||||OK...I 180'ed the Dis. now it will start. BUT.. the smoke is back and the exhaust smells like gas.. <B>VERY BAD!!!</B>..Im back where I started before. The Dis. is still not right. How can I find where it goes?<P>Thanks for the pic Oreif.. I double checked my order and its all good.||||reg||11
Z||000008||Indiana_resto_guy||11-10-2000||04:31 PM||||When all else fails;<BR>DRAW A PICTURE!  LOL (sorry C.!)<BR>Haze, have you attempted to set the timing yet? Sounds like you may be off only a tooth now. Try bringing the crank back to TDC (doesn't matter, either #1 or #4 compresssion stroke) make a mental note of the relationship of the afore mentioned locations on the dis. cap. Remove the cap and if the rotor is not pointing at either of these locations, pull it up and make it happen! Make sure that it is the WIDE mark on the balancer your lining up.<BR>LMK what goes!||||reg||1
Z||000009||Haze_Performance||11-10-2000||04:44 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Indiana_resto_guy:<BR><B>When all else fails;<BR>DRAW A PICTURE!  LOL (sorry C.!)<BR>Haze, have you attempted to set the timing yet? Sounds like you may be off only a tooth now. Try bringing the crank back to TDC (doesn't matter, either #1 or #4 compresssion stroke) make a mental note of the relationship of the afore mentioned locations on the dis. cap. Remove the cap and if the rotor is not pointing at either of these locations, pull it up and make it happen! Make sure that it is the WIDE mark on the balancer your lining up.<BR>LMK what goes!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Ok......... and away I go.... <P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/goodlogo1_1.gif">   <BR><B>"AHHHHH!!! All Fiero's don't start on fire you BONEHEAD!!"</B>||||reg||10
